{"id":"resp_84b73ef345064178","created_at":1795550827,"incomplete_details":null,"instructions":null,"metadata":null,"model":"gpt-oss-120b","object":"response","output":[{"id":"rs_a7b2db70ad45c793","summary":[],"type":"reasoning","content":[{"text":"We need to produce SHACL shapes that represent the regulatory source about ice classes. Use ontology: iceClass object property domain ship, range iceClassValue. Also need shapes for ship entities with iceClass property constrained to one of the six values (IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, III). Since the requirement lists allowed classes. We should create sh:NodeShape targeting ships (class ship). Use sh:targetClass maybe. Use sh:property with path iceClass and sh:in list of individuals.\n\nWe also need to capture textual description as sh:description maybe. Use sh:message.\n\nInclude source citations? Might include sh:annotationProperty for source, but not required.\n\nMake sure to include exact IRIs and no invented owners. Owner is ship class, already set.\n\nThus shape:\n\n<https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#shipShape> a sh:NodeShape; sh:targetClass <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#ship>; sh:property [ sh:path <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#iceClass>; sh:in ( <...IaSuper> <...Ia> <...Ib> <...Ic> <...Ii> <...Iii> ); sh:message \"Ship must have an ice class as defined in clause 1.8 of TRF-010.\" ].\n\nAdd sh:description with the clause text.\n\nAlso maybe shape for iceClassValue? Not needed.\n\nWe'll output <BEGIN_SHACL> line then Turtle then <END_SHACL>.\n\nMake sure prefixes: sh, rdf, rdfs, xsd, owl, nltl.\n\nLet's craft.\n\n","type":"reasoning_text"}],"encrypted_content":null,"status":null},{"id":"msg_8aa0fda63d43ec22","content":[{"annotations":[],"text":"<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh:    <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix rdf:   <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .\n@prefix rdfs:  <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .\n@prefix xsd:   <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix nltl:  <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\n# Shape that captures the ice‑class assignment requirement (TRF‑010, clause 1.8)\nnltl:ShipIceClassShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:description \"\"\"Under section 3 of the Act on the Ice Classes of Ships and Icebreaker Assistance (1121/2005), ships are assigned to ice classes as follows:\n1. ice class IA Super – ships capable of navigating in difficult ice conditions without icebreaker assistance;\n2. ice class IA – ships capable of navigating in difficult ice conditions with icebreaker assistance;\n3. ice class IB – ships capable of navigating in moderate ice conditions with icebreaker assistance;\n4. ice class IC – ships capable of navigating in light ice conditions with icebreaker assistance;\n5. ice class II – ships with a steel hull structurally fit for open‑sea navigation and able to navigate in very light ice using own propulsion;\n6. ice class III – ships that do not belong to the above classes.\"\"\" ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:iceClass ;\n        sh:in ( nltl:iceClassIaSuper nltl:iceClassIa nltl:iceClassIb nltl:iceClassIc nltl:iceClassIi nltl:iceClassIii ) ;\n        sh:message \"A ship must be assigned exactly one of the ice‑class values defined in clause 1.8 of TRF‑010 (IA Super, IA, IB, IC, II, III).\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>","type":"output_text","logprobs":null}],"role":"assistant","status":"completed","type":"message","phase":null}],"parallel_tool_calls":true,"temperature":1.0,"tool_choice":"none","tools":[],"top_p":1.0,"background":false,"max_output_tokens":16000,"max_tool_calls":null,"previous_response_id":null,"prompt":null,"prompt_cache_options":null,"prompt_cache_key":null,"prompt_cache_retention":null,"reasoning":null,"safety_identifier":null,"service_tier":"auto","status":"completed","text":null,"top_logprobs":null,"truncation":"disabled","usage":{"input_tokens":38536,"input_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":592,"cache_write_tokens":37936,"input_tokens_per_turn":[38536],"cached_tokens_per_turn":[592]},"output_tokens":803,"output_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":343,"tool_output_tokens":0,"output_tokens_per_turn":[803],"tool_output_tokens_per_turn":[0]},"total_tokens":39339},"user":null,"presence_penalty":0.0,"frequency_penalty":0.0,"kv_transfer_params":null,"ec_transfer_params":null,"input_messages":null,"output_messages":null}